<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flying Gang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1716">1716</a>–<a href="/years/1718">1718</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Flying Gang was the name given to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> based at Nassau in the Bahamas between about 1716 and 1718, the period known as the Republic of Pirates. Its members included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-hornigold">Benjamin Hornigold</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blackbeard">Edward Teach</a> (Blackbeard), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vane">Charles Vane</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-bellamy">Sam Bellamy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calico-jack">Calico Jack</a>. The community broke up after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodes-rogers">Woodes Rogers</a> arrived as royal governor in 1718 with a pardon, which many of them accepted.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flying-gang.jpg" alt="Flying Gang" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RootOfAllLight · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Flying_Gang.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
